## Pattern Summary

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    FACTORY METHOD                        │
│                                                          │
│  PizzaStore ──────────── createPizza() ◄── FACTORY      │
│      │                                     METHOD        │
│      ├── NYPizzaStore    ──► creates NY Pizzas           │
│      └── ChicagoPizzaStore ──► creates Chicago Pizzas   │
│                                                          │
│                    ABSTRACT FACTORY                      │
│                                                          │
│  PizzaIngredientFactory ◄─── used inside Pizza          │
│      ├── NYPizzaIngredientFactory                        │
│      └── ChicagoPizzaIngredientFactory                   │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

> **Key Difference:**
> - **Factory Method** → `createPizza()` in `PizzaStore` decides *which pizza* to make
> - **Abstract Factory** → `PizzaIngredientFactory` decides *which ingredients* to use inside the pizza

# Hello World Arduino Program

In Arduino, the "Hello World" equivalent is **blinking an LED** and/or **printing to Serial Monitor**.

---

## 1. Serial Monitor "Hello World"

```cpp
void setup() {
  Serial.begin(9600);  // Initialize serial communication at 9600 baud
}

void loop() {
  Serial.println("Hello, World!");  // Print message
  delay(1000);                       // Wait 1 second
}
```

---

## 2. Blink LED (Classic Arduino Hello World)

```cpp
void setup() {
  pinMode(LED_BUILTIN, OUTPUT);  // Set built-in LED pin as output
}

void loop() {
  digitalWrite(LED_BUILTIN, HIGH);  // Turn LED ON
  delay(1000);                       // Wait 1 second
  digitalWrite(LED_BUILTIN, LOW);   // Turn LED OFF
  delay(1000);                       // Wait 1 second
}
```

---

## 3. Combined Version

```cpp
void setup() {
  Serial.begin(9600);
  pinMode(LED_BUILTIN, OUTPUT);
  Serial.println("Arduino is ready!");
}

void loop() {
  digitalWrite(LED_BUILTIN, HIGH);
  Serial.println("Hello, World! - LED ON");
  delay(1000);

  digitalWrite(LED_BUILTIN, LOW);
  Serial.println("Hello, World! - LED OFF");
  delay(1000);
}
```

---

