## Visual Walkthrough

```
Operation    mainStack        minStack       Min
─────────────────────────────────────────────────
push(5)      [5]              [5]            5
push(3)      [5, 3]           [5, 3]         3
push(7)      [5, 3, 7]        [5, 3]         3   ← 7 > 3, skip
push(3)      [5, 3, 7, 3]     [5, 3, 3]      3   ← 3 == 3, push
push(2)      [5, 3, 7, 3, 2]  [5, 3, 3, 2]   2

pop()        [5, 3, 7, 3]     [5, 3, 3]      3   ← 2 removed from both
pop()        [5, 3, 7]        [5, 3]         3   ← 3 removed from both
pop()        [5, 3]           [5, 3]         3   ← 7 removed from main only
pop()        [5]              [5]            5   ← 3 removed from both
```

---

## Complexity Analysis

| Operation | Time | Space |
|-----------|------|-------|
| `push()`  | O(1) | O(n)  |
| `pop()`   | O(1) | O(1)  |
| `top()`   | O(1) | O(1)  |
| `getMin()`| O(1) | O(1)  |

> **Space Complexity:** O(n) overall — in worst case (descending input), both stacks hold n elements.

## Why `justify-content` Doesn't Work Here

`justify-content` is a **flexbox container property** - it only works when applied to the element that has `display: flex`. You're applying it to the **children** (`main > *`) instead of the **container** (`main`).

```css
/* ❌ Wrong - applying to children has no effect */
main > * {
    justify-content: center;
}

/* ✅ Correct - apply to the flex container */
main {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between; /* or space-around, space-evenly */
}
```

---

## For Equal Spacing on the Second Row

Since you want **equal distribution**, here are your options:

```css
main {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between; /* gaps between items */
    /* or */
    justify-content: space-around;  /* equal space around items */
    /* or */
    justify-content: space-evenly;  /* perfectly equal gaps */
}
```

### The difference:
| Value | Effect |
|-------|--------|
| `space-between` | No space on edges, equal gaps between |
| `space-around` | Half space on edges, equal space around each |
| `space-evenly` | Perfectly equal space everywhere |

---

> **Key Rule:** Flexbox properties like `justify-content`, `align-items`, and `flex-direction` always go on the **parent container**, not the children.

