# Using Vicuna-13B in .NET

Here are several approaches to use Vicuna-13B in .NET:

## Option 1: Using Ollama (Recommended - Easiest)

First, install Ollama and pull the model:
```bash
ollama pull vicuna
```

### Install NuGet Package
```bash
dotnet add package OllamaSharp
```

### C# Code
```csharp
using OllamaSharp;
using OllamaSharp.Models.Chat;

class Program
{
    static async Task Main(string[] args)
    {
        var ollama = new OllamaApiClient("http://localhost:11434");
        ollama.SelectedModel = "vicuna";

        // Simple generation
        await foreach (var token in ollama.GenerateAsync("Tell me about AI"))
        {
            Console.Write(token.Response);
        }

        Console.WriteLine();

        // Chat completion
        var chat = new Chat(ollama);
        var response = await chat.SendAsync("What is machine learning?");
        Console.WriteLine(response);
    }
}
```

---

## Option 2: Using LLamaSharp (Run Locally)

### Install NuGet Packages
```bash
dotnet add package LLamaSharp
dotnet add package LLamaSharp.Backend.Cpu   # For CPU
# OR
dotnet add package LLamaSharp.Backend.Cuda12 # For NVIDIA GPU
```

### Download Model
Download `vicuna-13b-v1.5.Q4_K_M.gguf` from HuggingFace.

### C# Code
```csharp
using LLama;
using LLama.Common;

class Program
{
    static async Task Main(string[] args)
    {
        string modelPath = "path/to/vicuna-13b-v1.5.Q4_K_M.gguf";

        var parameters = new ModelParams(modelPath)
        {
            ContextSize = 4096,
            GpuLayerCount = 35,  // Set to 0 for CPU only
            Seed = 1337,
            Threads = 8
        };

        using var model = LLamaWeights.LoadFromFile(parameters);
        using var context = model.CreateContext(parameters);
        var executor = new InteractiveExecutor(context);

        var chatHistory = new ChatHistory();
        chatHistory.AddMessage(AuthorRole.System,
            "You are a helpful AI assistant named Vicuna.");

        var session = new ChatSession(executor, chatHistory);

        var inferenceParams = new InferenceParams
        {
            MaxTokens = 512,
            AntiPrompts = new List<string> { "User:" }
        };

        Console.WriteLine("Chat with Vicuna (type 'exit' to quit)");
        Console.WriteLine("----------------------------------------");

        while (true)
        {
            Console.Write("You: ");
            string userInput = Console.ReadLine() ?? "";

            if (userInput.ToLower() == "exit") break;

            Console.Write("Vicuna: ");

            await foreach (var text in session.ChatAsync(
                new ChatHistory.Message(AuthorRole.User, userInput),
                inferenceParams))
            {
                Console.Write(text);
            }

            Console.WriteLine();
        }
    }
}
```

---

## Option 3: Using OpenAI-Compatible API (LM Studio / vLLM)

### Setup LM Studio
1. Download LM Studio
2. Load Vicuna-13B model
3. Start local server on `http://localhost:1234`

### Install NuGet Package
```bash
dotnet add package Azure.AI.OpenAI
# OR
dotnet add package OpenAI
```

### C# Code
```csharp
using Azure.AI.OpenAI;
using Azure;

class Program
{
    static async Task Main(string[] args)
    {
        // LM Studio / vLLM compatible endpoint
        var client = new OpenAIClient(
            new Uri("http://localhost:1234/v1"),
            new AzureKeyCredential("not-needed")
        );

        var chatCompletionsOptions = new ChatCompletionsOptions()
        {
            DeploymentName = "vicuna-13b",
            Messages =
            {
                new ChatRequestSystemMessage("You are Vicuna, a helpful AI assistant."),
                new ChatRequestUserMessage("Explain quantum computing in simple terms.")
            },
            MaxTokens = 512,
            Temperature = 0.7f,
            NucleusSamplingFactor = 0.9f
        };

        var response = await client.GetChatCompletionsAsync(chatCompletionsOptions);
        var message = response.Value.Choices[0].Message;
        Console.WriteLine($"Assistant: {message.Content}");
    }
}
```

